"We chose the Builder Pattern instead of the Singleton Pattern because our application requires creating multiple instances of complex objects with different configurations and optional properties.
The Builder Pattern provides a clean, step-by-step way to assemble these distinct objects while keeping them readable and immutable. In contrast, the Singleton Pattern is designed strictly to restrict a class to a single global instance across the entire application (such as a database connection manager), which does not fit our need for creating varied, independent objects."
